%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8b3ed0b47c7a6a94993706833db0821e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Team5_DialogueSequence
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Team5.qPCR.Runtime::Team5.qPCR.DialogueSequence
  entries:
  - Stage: 0
    Title: Inside the qPCR lab
    Instruction: You will configure a real-time PCR run, load Team 4's prepared plate,
      and explain the amplification result.
    Why: qPCR measures fluorescence during DNA copying, so the machine can show when
      amplification becomes detectable.
    Action: Begin lesson
    Focus: 0
  - Stage: 1
    Title: Meet your prepared plate
    Instruction: 'Review Team 4''s handoff: a filled, sealed, centrifuged 96-well
      plate with 28 active reactions.'
    Why: Each active well already contains supermix, both primers and its sample
      or control. The NTC has water instead of DNA. Open Reaction mix to see the
      teaching recipe.
    Action: Accept handoff
    Focus: 2
  - Stage: 2
    Title: Wake up the instrument
    Instruction: Switch on the qPCR instrument and wait for its touchscreen to become
      ready.
    Why: The instrument performs startup checks before it can heat, cool, or measure
      fluorescence.
    Action: Power on
    Focus: 1
  - Stage: 3
    Title: Configure the run
    Instruction: Check every value on the compact protocol panel. Correct settings
      protect the samples and make the results meaningful.
    Why: 'Each temperature performs a different job: separate DNA, attach primers,
      then build new DNA.'
    Action: Check settings
    Focus: 1
  - Stage: 4
    Title: Check the plate
    Instruction: Inspect the optical seal, confirm there are no bubbles, and align
      the A1 marker with the instrument.
    Why: Bubbles can disturb fluorescence readings, while A1 alignment keeps the
      digital plate map matched to the real wells.
    Action: Confirm inspection
    Focus: 2
  - Stage: 5
    Title: Seat the plate
    Instruction: Open the drawer, place the plate in the block, and close the drawer
      securely.
    Why: Firm placement gives every well equal thermal contact during cycling.
    Action: Load instrument
    Focus: 3
  - Stage: 6
    Title: Ready to start?
    Instruction: 'Complete the final check: protocol valid, plate inspected, A1 aligned,
      plate inserted, and drawer closed.'
    Why: The run stays locked until the machine and sample preparation checks all
      pass.
    Action: Start qPCR run
    Focus: 3
  - Stage: 7
    Title: DNA copying in progress
    Instruction: Watch 35 condensed cycles. Red separates DNA, blue lets primers
      bind, and green builds new strands.
    Why: SYBR dye detects double-stranded DNA, including unwanted products. The coloured
      animation is a diagram, not the real colour of the liquid.
    Action: "Running\u2026"
    Focus: 4
  - Stage: 8
    Title: Read the controls first
    Instruction: A valid run has a rising positive-control curve and a flat no-template-control
      curve. Choose the correct interpretation.
    Why: A rising NTC can mean contamination or primer-dimers. Controls and melt-curve
      evidence matter; a Cq number alone is not a diagnosis.
    Action: Controls passed
    Focus: 4
  - Stage: 9
    Title: Lesson complete
    Instruction: You configured, loaded, ran, and interpreted a complete educational
      qPCR workflow.
    Why: These representative curves teach the process but are not patient data and
      cannot be used for diagnosis.
    Action: Start again
    Focus: 0
